      "title": "Israeli parliament elects new speaker backed by Netanyahu’s opponents",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/17/israeli-parliament-elects-new-knesset-speaker-backed-netanyahus-opponents",
      "description": "<p>Knesset’s appointment of Matan Kahana marks step towards reversing policies of outgoing government</p><p>The Israeli parliament elected a new speaker on Tuesday, a key step toward rolling back policies passed by the outgoing government led by the prime minister, Benjamin Netanyahu.</p><p>The new speaker is Matan Kahana, an ally of <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/13/eisenkot-accuses-netanyahu-of-racist-campaign-against-israels-arab-minority\">Gadi Eisenkot</a>, the party leader currently <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/10/israeli-opposition-hurries-to-seize-control-as-new-knesset-is-sworn-in\">working to form the next government and replace Netanyahu</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/17/israeli-parliament-elects-new-knesset-speaker-backed-netanyahus-opponents\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
